. \"Vulnerability to Food Poverty in Nigeria\". *African Development Review*. **25** (3): 243–255. doi:10.1111/j.1467-8268.2013.12027.x.\n37. ↑ \"Nigeria - Multiple Indicator Cluster Survey 2016-2017\". *microdata.worldbank.org*. Retrieved 2020-05-29.\n38. ↑ Ogwumike, Fidelis; Ozughalu, Uche (1 March 2018). \"Empirical Evidence of Child Poverty and Deprivation in Nigeria\". *African Development Review*. **77** (1): 12–22. doi:10.1111/j.1467-8268.2013.12027.x. PMID 29294413.\n39. ↑ \"Wealth, poverty and rising violence\". *NRC*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n40. ↑ Dr Jideofor Adibe. \"Poverty Alleviation in Nigeria: Which Way Nigeria? :: Holler Africa - Make Yourself Heard!\". Holler Africa. Retrieved 2012-03-21.\n41. ↑ \"HISTORY OF AGRICULTURE IN NIGERIA - Agriculture Nigeria\". 2013-09-23. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n42. ↑ \"Events & Facts\". *www.cbn.gov.ng*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n43. ↑ \"RIVER BASIN DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITIES AND NIGERIA'S ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT SINCE 1960\". *ResearchGate*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n44. ↑ Owo, Chinweuba (2018-03-12). \"Rural Development in Nigeria: An Evaluation of the Performance of the Directorate of Food, Roads and Rural Infrastructures (DFRRI) in Nkanu L.G.A. of Anambra State | University of Nigeria, Nsukka Open Education Resources (OER)\". *oer.unn.edu.ng*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n45. ↑ \"Directorate of Food, Roads and Rural Infrastructures Act\". *www.ecolex.org*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n46. ↑ \"Nigeria - Fadama Development Project\". *projectsportal.afdb.org*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n47. ↑ \"Nigeria - Family Economic Advancement Programme (Establishment etc.) Decree 1997 (No. 11 of 1997)\". *www.ilo.org*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n48. ↑ \"Agricultural Transformation Agenda Support Programme. (ATASPS I)\". *Niger State Ministry of Agriculture*. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n49. ↑ \"Nigeria - Agricultural Transformation Agenda Support Program – Phase 1 (ATASP-1) - Executive SESA Summary\". *African Development Bank - Building today, a better Africa tomorrow*. 2019-05-28. Retrieved 2021-06-03.\n\n## Bibliography\n\n[edit]\n\n* \"African cities: Left behind\", *The Economist*, UK, 17 September 2016. (Mostly about Nigeria)\n\n## External links\n\n[edit]\n\n* OCLC WorldCat. Subject: Poverty - Nigeria (bibliography)","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":3670.6736449850723,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}